<Item XName="GlobalEqns" Attrib="14" Type="Equation">
<Text>FREQ=1e6;&#x000D;&#x000A;TIME=0.0;&#x000D;&#x000A;TEMPERATURE=16.85;&#x000D;&#x000A;Start_Time=0;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Start_Time, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Stop_Time=1;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Stop_Time, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Time_Spacing=.001;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Time_Spacing, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Num_Samples=1001;&#x000D;&#x000A;Sample_Rate=1000;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Sample_Rate, &apos;Hz&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Freq_Resolution=1;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Freq_Resolution, &apos;Hz&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Data_Persistence=0;&#x000D;&#x000A;Start_Time_SC=0;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Start_Time_SC, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Stop_Time_SC=1;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Stop_Time_SC, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Num_Samples_SC=1001;&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
<Item XName="BPMgr" Type="BPMgr">
<BPLines><T>Empty</T></BPLines>
<BPStates><T>Empty</T></BPStates></Item>
<Item XName="EqnBlock" Type="EqnBlock">
<Lang><T>Int</T><D>1</D></Lang></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
<Name>Courier New</Name>
<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" />
<Item XName="VarBlock" Type="VarBlock" /></Item>
<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT color=#0000ff size=6&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in&quot; class=MsoTitle align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=5&gt;MSR Base Station Maximum Output Power&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This example demonstrates how to measure the MSR base station maximum output power according to clause 6.2 of 3GPP TS 37.141.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 9pt&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Output power of the Base Station is the mean power delivered to a load with resistance equal to the nominal load impedance of the transmitter. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The maximum carrier output power, P&lt;SUB&gt;max,c&lt;/SUB&gt; of the Base Station is the mean power level measured at the antenna connector during the transmitter ON period for a specific carrier in a specified reference condition. &lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bidi-font-family: &apos;v4.2.0&apos;&quot; lang=EN-GB&gt;The test purpose is to verify the accuracy of the maximum carrier output power across the frequency range and under normal and extreme conditions for all transmitters in the BS&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;In this example, five LTE signals and six WCDMA signals are combined at Fc = 2.14e9 Hz in MSR Band 1 (2110MHz - 2170MHz) as defined in Table 4.4-1 of&amp;nbsp;3GPP TS 37.104 using SingalCombiner part.&amp;nbsp;Equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration&lt;/EM&gt; specifies the used MSR Band and the signal configurations of each carrier e.g. sampling rate, bandwidth and power.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The spectrum graph &quot;MSR_spec_Power&quot; shows the combined spectrum, while&amp;nbsp;the spectrum graph &quot;MSR_spec_Power with individual spectrums&quot; shows the combined spectrum along with individual standard spectrum.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Table &quot;OutputPower_dBm&quot; shows the measured carrier output power caculated in equation &lt;EM&gt;PowerCalculation&lt;/EM&gt;. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;TRY THIS:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;Change &lt;EM&gt;GCType&lt;/EM&gt; in &lt;EM&gt;Amplifier&lt;/EM&gt; in &lt;EM&gt;Design1 to add PA nonlinearities.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;Change MSR band in equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;by setting F_BWlow, F_BWhigh and F_BWmid.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Change the signal configuration in equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Specify different LTE carriers and WCDMA carriers to measure by setting &lt;EM&gt;MeasLTECarrierIndex&lt;/EM&gt; and &lt;EM&gt;MeasWCDMACarrierIndex&lt;/EM&gt; in equation &lt;EM&gt;PowerCalculation.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;</Text>
